1
00:00:08,258 --> 00:00:10,927
<i>Easton!</i>

2
00:00:12,137 --> 00:00:14,973
-[crowd chanting] Easton! Easton! Easton!
-[man] Let's go!

3
00:00:16,307 --> 00:00:19,728
-[chanting continues]
-[ominous music playing]

4
00:00:29,779 --> 00:00:32,240
[whirring]

5
00:00:47,338 --> 00:00:50,842
[chanting continues]
Easton! Easton! Easton!

6
00:00:53,053 --> 00:00:56,598
{\an8}["Doing It for the Country"
by Vincent's Last Summer playing]

7
00:00:59,517 --> 00:01:00,643
[Teagan giggling]

8
00:01:04,689 --> 00:01:08,443
There's nothing hotter
than the smell of bleach. [laughing]

9
00:01:09,319 --> 00:01:10,487
Less talking.

10
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:13,239
{\an8}[movement in other room]

11
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:18,078
{\an8}-Maybe we should go somewhere else.
-Yeah.

12
00:01:18,953 --> 00:01:20,955
{\an8}<i>♪ I'm doing it for the country ♪</i>

13
00:01:21,039 --> 00:01:22,916
{\an8}<i>♪ Just give me one more reason ♪</i>

14
00:01:22,999 --> 00:01:25,001
<i>♪ Call it hate, but you call it treason ♪</i>

15
00:01:25,085 --> 00:01:26,961
<i>♪ There only is one demon ♪</i>

16
00:01:27,045 --> 00:01:29,130
<i>♪ Can't do bunker drills, can't afford ♪</i>

17
00:01:29,214 --> 00:01:31,424
<i>-♪Just give me one more reason ♪</i>
-[phone beeping]

18
00:01:31,508 --> 00:01:33,134
-[music stops]
-You gotta be kidding me.

19
00:01:35,428 --> 00:01:37,597
-Five more minutes.
-No, okay?

20
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:39,891
-There's a regatta in two hours.
-What?

21
00:01:39,974 --> 00:01:42,143
The team's gonna be here soon.

22
00:01:43,061 --> 00:01:45,730
I'll leave first in case anyone's outside.

23
00:01:46,272 --> 00:01:47,232
Okay.

24
00:01:49,734 --> 00:01:51,903
Wait. I think you have something… there.

25
00:01:51,986 --> 00:01:53,196
[music starts again]

26
00:01:53,279 --> 00:01:57,534
<i>♪ Everywhere I go</i>
<i>I see your face up on billboards now ♪</i>

27
00:01:57,617 --> 00:02:01,287
<i>♪ I'm gonna take it all</i>
<i>A privatized free-for-all ♪</i>

28
00:02:01,371 --> 00:02:05,333
<i>♪ I had to get a train and it was</i>
<i>An hour and a half delayed now ♪</i>

29
00:02:05,416 --> 00:02:09,003
<i>♪ I think my time is up</i>
<i>Occupation ending, give it up now ♪</i>

30
00:02:09,629 --> 00:02:10,505
[sighs]

31
00:02:11,089 --> 00:02:14,050
And here we go.

32
00:02:15,885 --> 00:02:18,263
<i>♪ I do it all for you ♪</i>

33
00:02:20,932 --> 00:02:22,767
Mad, wanna help me bring this stuff in?

34
00:02:22,851 --> 00:02:24,060
Okay, but you owe me.

35
00:02:24,936 --> 00:02:26,146
I put a roof over your head,

36
00:02:26,229 --> 00:02:28,273
provide you
with unlimited high-top Chucks.

37
00:02:28,356 --> 00:02:30,733
-But we ain't even yet?
-Close, but not yet.

38
00:02:35,446 --> 00:02:37,323
I'll keep that in mind.

39
00:02:39,576 --> 00:02:41,786
-Hey.
-Oh, hey.

40
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:45,081
-How are you feeling about today?
-Yeah. I like our chances.

41
00:02:46,124 --> 00:02:48,084
What, uh, happened with you and Teagan?

42
00:02:48,168 --> 00:02:51,045
I didn't see you guys
at the end of the dance. Did it go well?

43
00:02:51,671 --> 00:02:53,882
No. It's not happening.

44
00:02:55,466 --> 00:02:58,970
Here. Let me help you.
Here, I'll take this.

45
00:02:59,053 --> 00:03:00,471
-Do you want to talk about it?
-Uh…

46
00:03:01,014 --> 00:03:03,558
No, I don't. It's not gonna work.

47
00:03:05,143 --> 00:03:06,352
Okay, it's fine.

48
00:03:08,313 --> 00:03:10,356
[Madison] Wait, why is the truck for sale?

49
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:11,858
Is something going on?

50
00:03:11,941 --> 00:03:13,943
[quiet, somber music playing]

51
00:03:14,777 --> 00:03:15,987
The shop's in trouble.

52
00:03:16,070 --> 00:03:19,157
Dad laid off the other mechanics,
and I've been picking up the slack.

53
00:03:20,617 --> 00:03:21,618
That's tough.

54
00:03:22,243 --> 00:03:23,620
Is there anything I can do?

55
00:03:23,703 --> 00:03:25,371
I just… I gotta get through this.

56
00:03:27,123 --> 00:03:28,291
-Okay.
-[object crunching]

57
00:03:28,374 --> 00:03:30,293
[Madison gasps] Oh, oh no!

58
00:03:38,134 --> 00:03:39,510
I'm so sorry.

59
00:03:41,095 --> 00:03:42,805
Don't worry, it's fine. It's okay.

60
00:03:42,889 --> 00:03:44,515
["Hold Me Close"
by Russell Chimes playing]

61
00:03:44,599 --> 00:03:46,935
-[Noah] Prepare yourselves for tonight.
-There gonna be a DJ?

62
00:03:47,018 --> 00:03:48,770
I heard Diplo came last year.

63
00:03:48,853 --> 00:03:50,688
Two years ago,
we took the yacht to Deer Island.

64
00:03:50,772 --> 00:03:52,565
-Partied on the beach all night.
-Sweet!

65
00:03:52,649 --> 00:03:53,900
[Teagan] Hey!

66
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:56,152
-Yo. Smoothie up.
-Thanks.

67
00:03:56,236 --> 00:03:58,321
You guys talking about
the regatta after-party?

68
00:03:58,404 --> 00:03:59,322
Hell yeah!

69
00:03:59,405 --> 00:04:02,700
Noah's planning it this year,
and he has a lot to live up to.

70
00:04:02,784 --> 00:04:04,661
[Noah] You will not
be disappointed, friends.

71
00:04:04,744 --> 00:04:06,079
Hey. Morning, boys.

72
00:04:06,162 --> 00:04:08,373
-[team] Morning.
-[Josh exhales]

73
00:04:09,916 --> 00:04:10,917
Morning, Teagan.

74
00:04:12,961 --> 00:04:14,587
Josh. Sip-sip.

75
00:04:17,548 --> 00:04:18,758
Hey!

76
00:04:26,599 --> 00:04:27,684
[Richard] Josh.

77
00:04:28,851 --> 00:04:29,978
Dad.

78
00:04:30,061 --> 00:04:32,689
I thought you were supposed to be
with Mom and Granddad.

79
00:04:32,772 --> 00:04:35,733
They're looking for
a good spot to watch from.

80
00:04:37,694 --> 00:04:38,987
Son.

81
00:04:40,154 --> 00:04:41,656
I have some hard news.

82
00:04:43,324 --> 00:04:46,828
Dad promoted Karina
to President of Luxury Travel.

83
00:04:46,911 --> 00:04:48,538
Wasn't that was supposed to be your job?

84
00:04:49,372 --> 00:04:50,373
Yeah.

85
00:04:51,249 --> 00:04:52,292
She scooped me.

86
00:04:53,668 --> 00:04:54,836
That's not good.

87
00:04:57,714 --> 00:04:59,841
I need a win here, Josh.

88
00:04:59,924 --> 00:05:01,259
[foreboding music playing]

89
00:05:01,342 --> 00:05:02,343
You're in stroke.

90
00:05:02,427 --> 00:05:05,138
A win will put us
back on top in Dad's mind.

91
00:05:06,347 --> 00:05:07,348
Right.

92
00:05:09,183 --> 00:05:11,269
I'd, uh, better go join him.

93
00:05:11,352 --> 00:05:13,354
[tense music playing]

94
00:05:18,943 --> 00:05:19,944
[exhales]

95
00:05:27,035 --> 00:05:28,036
Morning.

96
00:05:29,454 --> 00:05:32,373
Coach asked for the slow cooker.
I left it on the counter.

97
00:05:33,249 --> 00:05:35,126
-Okay. Thanks.
-Yeah.

98
00:05:35,209 --> 00:05:39,047
Is there, uh… anything else
you wanna talk about?

99
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:40,423
Yo.

100
00:05:41,424 --> 00:05:42,425
No.

101
00:05:43,801 --> 00:05:45,261
One whole word.

102
00:05:46,220 --> 00:05:50,099
Still more communicative than your texts.

103
00:05:51,392 --> 00:05:52,226
Mm.

104
00:05:52,852 --> 00:05:54,562
[Perry whispering] Something's going on.

105
00:05:54,645 --> 00:05:55,855
Cam.

106
00:05:57,815 --> 00:06:00,109
I know you had a hard time at the dance,

107
00:06:00,193 --> 00:06:03,780
and I am trying to give you your space,
but you know you could talk to me.

108
00:06:04,781 --> 00:06:05,782
Yeah, I know.

109
00:06:07,492 --> 00:06:08,576
Thanks.

110
00:06:13,664 --> 00:06:15,041
[sighs]

111
00:06:15,124 --> 00:06:16,584
-Go on.
-Okay.

112
00:06:16,667 --> 00:06:18,628
[intriguing music playing]

113
00:06:18,711 --> 00:06:21,672
Hey, girl. You and Cam
didn't come to the after-party.

114
00:06:21,756 --> 00:06:23,966
Now the vibe's all formal. What's up?

115
00:06:24,050 --> 00:06:26,636
You guys trying to sneak around,
keep things profesh?

116
00:06:28,096 --> 00:06:29,138
No comment.

117
00:06:30,139 --> 00:06:32,350
So… yes?

118
00:06:35,478 --> 00:06:37,855
Okay. Good chat.

119
00:06:42,026 --> 00:06:43,694
-[Noah] So?
-She gave me nothing.

120
00:06:43,778 --> 00:06:45,696
-Dude.
-[Perry] Yeah.

121
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:48,449
[Hayden] All right, crew, huddle up.
Bring it in, bring it in.

122
00:06:52,995 --> 00:06:55,331
Last regatta before the Haverford Cup.

123
00:06:55,415 --> 00:06:59,585
If we place here, we can secure our spot,
giving us a shot at the podium.

124
00:06:59,669 --> 00:07:01,671
The first time in ten years.

125
00:07:01,754 --> 00:07:03,965
[team cheering and exclaiming]

126
00:07:04,048 --> 00:07:08,970
Y'all feel good about that? You should!
Because this race is yours for the taking.

127
00:07:09,053 --> 00:07:11,055
Yeah, Westvale is toast!

128
00:07:11,139 --> 00:07:15,101
No, wait. They are past toast.
They are ash. They're…

129
00:07:15,184 --> 00:07:16,185
-Um…
-Tephra.

130
00:07:16,269 --> 00:07:17,812
What the hell is a tephra?

131
00:07:17,895 --> 00:07:20,898
-Material produced by volcanic eruption.
-Isn't that just lava?

132
00:07:20,982 --> 00:07:22,859
Okay, losing the plot here.

133
00:07:22,942 --> 00:07:24,402
-Coach?
-Thank you.

134
00:07:24,944 --> 00:07:26,237
Listen, a hot streak is great.

135
00:07:26,320 --> 00:07:29,449
But Westvale's gonna do
whatever it takes to get back on top.

136
00:07:29,532 --> 00:07:32,827
So one clean drive after another,
and we can take this thing, yeah?

137
00:07:32,910 --> 00:07:34,871
[team] Yes, Coach!

138
00:07:34,954 --> 00:07:36,122
All right. Regis?

139
00:07:36,205 --> 00:07:37,123
[both] Yeah?

140
00:07:37,999 --> 00:07:39,000
I meant Josh.

141
00:07:39,709 --> 00:07:42,795
Let's take it out easy today, okay?
It's a head race, not a sprint.

142
00:07:42,879 --> 00:07:43,754
You got it?

143
00:07:44,422 --> 00:07:45,256
Yes, Coach.

144
00:07:45,339 --> 00:07:46,299
[Hayden] Okay.

145
00:07:46,924 --> 00:07:49,135
Go change,
do whatever prep you need to do,

146
00:07:49,218 --> 00:07:52,263
and I will see you
out on the tarmac in 60.

147
00:07:52,763 --> 00:07:53,764
Let's get to work.

148
00:07:54,891 --> 00:07:59,103
-[Teagan] Great.
-And just a quick remindy about the party.

149
00:07:59,187 --> 00:08:02,398
It's gonna be both the bee's knees
and the cat's meow.

150
00:08:03,357 --> 00:08:05,693
I'm getting a bad feeling
about this party.

151
00:08:05,776 --> 00:08:07,695
Me too, man.
I'm allergic to bees and cats.

152
00:08:07,778 --> 00:08:08,613
[phone buzzing]

153
00:08:08,696 --> 00:08:11,240
[Teagan] Remember,
back your blades in at the catch.

154
00:08:11,949 --> 00:08:13,951
Okay! Let's go!

155
00:08:14,035 --> 00:08:14,994
[team assenting]

156
00:08:15,077 --> 00:08:16,245
[buzzing continues]

157
00:08:17,622 --> 00:08:18,831
Hi.

158
00:08:18,915 --> 00:08:20,917
[Logan] <i>I'm here a little early.</i>

159
00:08:23,044 --> 00:08:24,420
I'll see you in five.

160
00:08:30,426 --> 00:08:31,427
Hey.

161
00:08:32,428 --> 00:08:33,721
Congrats on being back in stroke.

162
00:08:33,804 --> 00:08:34,972
Hey.

163
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:37,058
Thanks for your support.

164
00:08:37,683 --> 00:08:38,976
Must be a lot of pressure though.

165
00:08:39,936 --> 00:08:41,062
And why's that?

166
00:08:41,145 --> 00:08:43,397
'Cause when I was in stroke, we won.

167
00:08:43,481 --> 00:08:46,067
[tense music playing]

168
00:08:47,193 --> 00:08:48,402
Don't screw it up.

169
00:08:51,155 --> 00:08:54,575
[crowd cheering and whooping]

170
00:09:08,339 --> 00:09:10,132
Yo. Sunglasses are broken.

171
00:09:10,216 --> 00:09:11,801
Yeah, taped them up.

172
00:09:11,884 --> 00:09:14,345
It's regulation.
The whole team has to wear the same thing.

173
00:09:14,428 --> 00:09:16,514
-Yours can't be broken.
-What do you want me to do?

174
00:09:16,597 --> 00:09:17,598
You don't have a backup?

175
00:09:17,682 --> 00:09:20,142
Not all of us have an extra
$300 lying around, jackass.

176
00:09:20,226 --> 00:09:21,602
Okay.

177
00:09:22,395 --> 00:09:24,897
But you can't go out like that.
We won't match.

178
00:09:25,815 --> 00:09:27,441
Then we won't match.

179
00:09:28,859 --> 00:09:29,860
Fine.

180
00:09:30,570 --> 00:09:36,158
I'll tell the whole team
that we're all going without sunglasses.

181
00:09:40,121 --> 00:09:41,872
Yo, you think you deserve to be in stroke.

182
00:09:43,374 --> 00:09:44,500
You don't.

183
00:09:45,418 --> 00:09:46,377
Excuse me?

184
00:09:46,460 --> 00:09:51,132
I have better technique than you.
I'm faster than you. I'm just better.

185
00:09:51,215 --> 00:09:53,384
Hey. Coach picked me.

186
00:09:53,884 --> 00:09:57,680
I have been working my ass off.
I absolutely deserve to be in that seat.

187
00:09:57,763 --> 00:10:00,057
No, you don't. You were born lucky.

188
00:10:01,017 --> 00:10:02,727
And you need to figure that out.

189
00:10:04,228 --> 00:10:06,355
Maybe everything you have,
you don't deserve.

190
00:10:06,856 --> 00:10:11,193
[dramatic music playing]

191
00:10:12,737 --> 00:10:15,656
[crowd chanting] Easton! Easton! Easton!

192
00:10:16,365 --> 00:10:19,452
Easton! Easton! Easton!

193
00:10:22,079 --> 00:10:24,957
-[chanting continues in background]
-[Teagan laughs]

194
00:10:25,041 --> 00:10:26,292
-Thank you.
-All right!

195
00:10:26,375 --> 00:10:27,209
Everybody here?

196
00:10:28,294 --> 00:10:29,879
Coxie, count us in.

197
00:10:30,421 --> 00:10:31,422
All right.

198
00:10:32,089 --> 00:10:33,466
Easton on three!

199
00:10:33,549 --> 00:10:35,926
-[all] One, two, Easton!
-Let's go!

200
00:10:36,010 --> 00:10:37,094
Crew, go get your boat.

201
00:10:37,178 --> 00:10:38,304
[Teagan] Go!

202
00:10:39,472 --> 00:10:42,433
[tense music playing]

203
00:10:52,026 --> 00:10:54,362
[woman on PA] Easton Prep, on standby.

204
00:10:55,488 --> 00:10:56,906
Back in the saddle.

205
00:10:57,657 --> 00:10:58,658
Feeling good?

206
00:11:00,368 --> 00:11:01,661
Let's do this.

207
00:11:03,788 --> 00:11:04,830
Paddle up.

208
00:11:08,626 --> 00:11:11,087
[woman] Easton Prep, on the paddle.

209
00:11:11,170 --> 00:11:13,172
[Teagan] Legs!

210
00:11:13,255 --> 00:11:17,426
Starting off strong! Here we go!

211
00:11:17,510 --> 00:11:18,844
-Easton, go!
-[horn blows]

212
00:11:18,928 --> 00:11:24,684
And pull! Let's go, Eagles! Come on!
Starting strong! Pull!

213
00:11:24,767 --> 00:11:28,979
[fast-paced music playing]

214
00:11:29,063 --> 00:11:30,856
Keep it up! Keep it up!

215
00:11:36,904 --> 00:11:41,117
Go! Legs! Pull!

216
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:42,576
-Oh!
-[team exclaiming]

217
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:43,661
It went off.

218
00:11:43,744 --> 00:11:45,371
-[Cam] What?
-[Crabcatcher] What was that?

219
00:11:45,454 --> 00:11:46,455
[Ryder] What's going on?

220
00:11:47,456 --> 00:11:48,999
-My oar!
-[Noah] Guys!

221
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:50,793
It just snapped.

222
00:11:51,335 --> 00:11:52,336
[Quaid] No way!

223
00:11:53,379 --> 00:11:54,964
-[Josh groans]
-[sighing]

224
00:11:58,175 --> 00:12:00,761
[Lana] Easton Prep, you are disqualified.

225
00:12:00,845 --> 00:12:01,846
God!

226
00:12:02,346 --> 00:12:04,348
[somber music playing]

227
00:12:10,062 --> 00:12:11,397
[Hayden] Okay, guys.

228
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:14,275
I know this is not
how we wanted this to end.

229
00:12:14,358 --> 00:12:16,986
But sometimes, it's just not your day.

230
00:12:17,069 --> 00:12:18,821
But we should have had that race.

231
00:12:18,904 --> 00:12:20,114
We still have a chance.

232
00:12:20,197 --> 00:12:22,992
We're disqualified from the race,
but not from making the Haverford Cup.

233
00:12:23,075 --> 00:12:25,536
If Cedarside and Lakeview
don't place in the top three,

234
00:12:25,619 --> 00:12:27,246
we'll still qualify.

235
00:12:27,329 --> 00:12:31,167
We just have to wait for the results
for the other teams to come in. Okay?

236
00:12:31,876 --> 00:12:36,422
Have a good time tonight.
You've earned it. Keep your head up.

237
00:12:41,010 --> 00:12:44,180
Man, if our oar didn't break,
we could've been on that podium.

238
00:12:44,263 --> 00:12:46,140
It was a fluke. It happens.

239
00:12:46,223 --> 00:12:48,517
[Noah] You know what else happens?

240
00:12:50,811 --> 00:12:53,731
-Our after-party.
-[team] Yeah!

241
00:12:53,814 --> 00:12:56,776
[clapping]

242
00:12:56,859 --> 00:12:59,653
-[Ryder] Who's the musical guest?
-[Perry] Shit. Are we seeing Bad Bunny?

243
00:12:59,737 --> 00:13:04,617
Indeed, we will be in the proximity
of something very bad.

244
00:13:04,700 --> 00:13:07,077
-Hey!
-Yeah, let's get bad, baby.

245
00:13:07,161 --> 00:13:10,456
And here it is. Our night's marquee event…

246
00:13:11,749 --> 00:13:13,292
a murder mystery.

247
00:13:13,918 --> 00:13:15,461
-Uh-oh.
-Oh, hell no.

248
00:13:15,544 --> 00:13:16,587
Why?

249
00:13:16,670 --> 00:13:20,966
Our tale begins in an era
marked by greed and rebellion.

250
00:13:21,050 --> 00:13:26,096
America's moral compass,
once steady, now spins recklessly.

251
00:13:26,597 --> 00:13:28,015
I bring you all…

252
00:13:29,934 --> 00:13:31,519
to the Roaring '20s!

253
00:13:37,483 --> 00:13:39,652
Now, we've all read <i>The Great Gatsby</i>.

254
00:13:39,735 --> 00:13:40,569
[all] We did?

255
00:13:40,653 --> 00:13:42,780
We did. It was on last year's curriculum.

256
00:13:42,863 --> 00:13:45,616
Okay, well, Crabby and I
have read <i>The Great Gatsby</i>.

257
00:13:45,699 --> 00:13:48,953
Now, during Prohibition,
alcohol was forbidden.

258
00:13:49,036 --> 00:13:50,329
Is this a dry party?

259
00:13:51,038 --> 00:13:52,122
Yeah, obviously.

260
00:13:52,206 --> 00:13:54,458
-[team moaning]
-Oh, no.

261
00:13:54,542 --> 00:13:59,046
[stammers] But the Roaring '20s
gave birth to jazz.

262
00:13:59,129 --> 00:14:01,966
-And cabaret.
-Yeah.

263
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:03,384
Ugh.

264
00:14:03,467 --> 00:14:05,928
-A friggin' murder mystery.
-[Baloo] A dry murder mystery.

265
00:14:06,011 --> 00:14:07,304
Why do you hate us, Noah?

266
00:14:07,388 --> 00:14:08,681
[Teagan] Guys, come on.

267
00:14:08,764 --> 00:14:13,644
Noah spent a lot of time
planning this party, so… go ahead.

268
00:14:15,396 --> 00:14:16,397
[clears throat]

269
00:14:16,480 --> 00:14:18,649
-[dramatic music playing]
-A heinous crime occurred

270
00:14:18,732 --> 00:14:20,693
-in this opulent mansion.
-[crunching]

271
00:14:20,776 --> 00:14:22,319
-[music stops]
-Quaid, not right now.

272
00:14:22,403 --> 00:14:23,404
What?

273
00:14:27,283 --> 00:14:28,325
Okay.

274
00:14:28,409 --> 00:14:30,035
-[music restarts]
-A heinous crime occurred

275
00:14:30,119 --> 00:14:32,079
inside this opulent mansion.

276
00:14:32,621 --> 00:14:35,708
The murder of a reclusive dowager duchess.

277
00:14:36,375 --> 00:14:38,669
The weapon? An oyster shucker.

278
00:14:38,752 --> 00:14:42,172
The motive? Her priceless ruby necklace.

279
00:14:42,756 --> 00:14:43,674
Stolen.

280
00:14:44,425 --> 00:14:49,555
Now, you'll all find your characters
and costumes by your changeroom cubbies.

281
00:14:49,638 --> 00:14:51,140
Disperse!

282
00:14:51,223 --> 00:14:52,600
-Ah!
-[music stops]

283
00:14:58,981 --> 00:15:03,986
Boys, come on. Let's… disperse! Disperse!

284
00:15:04,069 --> 00:15:07,114
Let's stop waiting for the results
and go solve a murder!

285
00:15:07,197 --> 00:15:08,574
It's gonna be great!

286
00:15:09,074 --> 00:15:10,659
[team grumbling]

287
00:15:10,743 --> 00:15:12,703
-I'm sure.
-[grumbling continues]

288
00:15:12,786 --> 00:15:14,288
[Quaid] That makes a lot of sense.

289
00:15:14,788 --> 00:15:16,957
I worked really hard on this.
It's gonna be fun.

290
00:15:17,041 --> 00:15:19,460
-[grumbling continues]
-[Noah laughs awkwardly]

291
00:15:20,794 --> 00:15:21,795
Yes.

292
00:15:27,593 --> 00:15:31,597
Hey, Dad. Uh, trying you again
'cause I haven't heard back from you.

293
00:15:32,097 --> 00:15:33,390
I, uh…

294
00:15:33,891 --> 00:15:36,060
I know the race
didn't go the way we needed.

295
00:15:36,894 --> 00:15:38,687
I'm sorry that I let you down.

296
00:15:38,771 --> 00:15:40,773
[somber music playing]

297
00:15:44,526 --> 00:15:45,361
[sighs]

298
00:15:50,032 --> 00:15:51,700
Well, I'll be…

299
00:15:51,784 --> 00:15:54,036
[mysterious string music playing]

300
00:15:54,119 --> 00:15:56,372
Who in this dastardly rogues' gallery

301
00:15:56,455 --> 00:15:59,959
is responsible for the slaying
of the innocent dowager?

302
00:16:00,042 --> 00:16:02,628
I've hidden clues all around this mansion

303
00:16:02,711 --> 00:16:06,590
that you and your fellow suspects
must gather.

304
00:16:06,674 --> 00:16:07,841
Announce yourselves!

305
00:16:10,886 --> 00:16:11,971
Guys, come on.

306
00:16:18,894 --> 00:16:20,521
"I'm Carl."

307
00:16:21,021 --> 00:16:25,943
"A speakeasy steward
with dreams of a better life."

308
00:16:26,485 --> 00:16:28,696
-Wait, I'm a janitor?
-Ooh, with a selfless heart.

309
00:16:28,779 --> 00:16:31,991
Or one filled with bloodlust.

310
00:16:32,533 --> 00:16:38,038
"I am Eleanor Ramshine.
A wealthy flapper who is…

311
00:16:39,748 --> 00:16:42,209
judgy and into hats."

312
00:16:42,292 --> 00:16:43,585
-What a typecast.
-[Noah] Yes!

313
00:16:43,669 --> 00:16:48,882
You two will begin in the kitchen
after a clandestine necking party.

314
00:16:48,966 --> 00:16:50,300
-Necking?
-Wait, what's necking?

315
00:16:51,010 --> 00:16:53,429
"Baloo and I are big sluggers."

316
00:16:53,512 --> 00:16:56,515
"Two mobster henchmen
to one of Chicago's unfinest."

317
00:16:56,598 --> 00:16:58,892
[imitating gangster]
We're gonna break your legs!

318
00:16:58,976 --> 00:17:02,187
Speedy Sinclair. Newspaper boy.

319
00:17:03,147 --> 00:17:06,191
-Amelia Faye. Silent film star.
-[Teagan clears throat]

320
00:17:06,275 --> 00:17:07,609
You're with…

321
00:17:07,693 --> 00:17:12,197
Mr. Brandenburg, a federal agent.
You two will begin in the boat sheds.

322
00:17:12,281 --> 00:17:15,034
And last but not least…

323
00:17:18,954 --> 00:17:21,749
Oil magnate Edward Harold.

324
00:17:23,083 --> 00:17:24,543
Who is also…

325
00:17:24,626 --> 00:17:26,795
-[glass clattering]
-…a secret moonshine brewer.

326
00:17:26,879 --> 00:17:28,672
[team]

327
00:17:28,756 --> 00:17:31,717
-Yeah!
-Wait up, Quaid, that is not on your card.

328
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:34,553
Yeah, the speakeasy is open for business.

329
00:17:34,636 --> 00:17:36,346
I got one for each of you. Come here.

330
00:17:36,430 --> 00:17:37,556
This is mine. Don't take it.

331
00:17:37,639 --> 00:17:39,641
[Noah] Quaid,
where did you even get these? Stop.

332
00:17:39,725 --> 00:17:41,268
This is my emergency stash.

333
00:17:41,351 --> 00:17:42,519
[Baloo laughing mischievously]

334
00:17:42,603 --> 00:17:47,191
Okay, uh, uh, guys,
just don't forget about the clues, okay?

335
00:17:47,274 --> 00:17:49,359
There's gonna be a new discovery
in round two!

336
00:17:49,443 --> 00:17:51,570
[rower] Yeah!

337
00:17:55,991 --> 00:18:00,746
[in fake English accent] Okay,
Mr. Brandenburg. What's the clue again?

338
00:18:00,829 --> 00:18:03,248
Well, let's see, Amelia Faye.

339
00:18:03,332 --> 00:18:04,416
[Teagan laughs]

340
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:08,003
"A shining three is where you'll find me."

341
00:18:08,796 --> 00:18:12,216
Hey, Noah sits in the three seat.

342
00:18:13,133 --> 00:18:16,678
Maybe our next clue
is in one of the shells.

343
00:18:16,762 --> 00:18:18,388
[Teagan laughing]

344
00:18:18,472 --> 00:18:19,765
Yes.

345
00:18:24,812 --> 00:18:25,813
Ah.

346
00:18:27,022 --> 00:18:28,107
Bad break.

347
00:18:28,899 --> 00:18:29,942
Yeah.

348
00:18:31,777 --> 00:18:34,696
-[Josh sighs]
-Did your dad call you back yet?

349
00:18:35,364 --> 00:18:36,657
No.

350
00:18:36,740 --> 00:18:40,285
And I don't think
he's going to anytime soon.

351
00:18:44,123 --> 00:18:49,294
Hey. Josh, come on.
There's nothing you could have done, okay?

352
00:18:50,045 --> 00:18:51,713
Don't beat yourself up.

353
00:18:52,214 --> 00:18:53,715
We'll get 'em next time.

354
00:18:55,134 --> 00:18:56,343
Okay.

355
00:18:59,471 --> 00:19:00,514
Huh.

356
00:19:00,597 --> 00:19:02,391
Wait a second.

357
00:19:03,767 --> 00:19:04,893
What?

358
00:19:05,394 --> 00:19:08,147
-That didn't just break on its own.
-[sinister music playing]

359
00:19:08,230 --> 00:19:10,149
That's sawed through.

360
00:19:10,232 --> 00:19:11,441
What?

361
00:19:17,197 --> 00:19:18,448
[Teagan] The oar was sabotaged.

362
00:19:18,532 --> 00:19:21,743
Look. It was cut part way through
so it'd break during the race.

363
00:19:21,827 --> 00:19:23,412
-Shit.
-Who would do this?

364
00:19:23,495 --> 00:19:26,206
-You can't be serious.
-We've stumbled upon a real mystery.

365
00:19:26,290 --> 00:19:29,543
It was cut with an electric saw.
It's pretty common. Every team has one.

366
00:19:29,626 --> 00:19:32,796
-Well, why the hell would someone do this?
-[Ryder] Well, isn't it obvious?

367
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:36,008
Some Westvale scumbag is probably
trying to keep us off the podium.

368
00:19:36,091 --> 00:19:36,967
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

369
00:19:37,050 --> 00:19:40,888
There's no way they could've done that.
Our oars were in sight during the regatta,

370
00:19:40,971 --> 00:19:44,391
so someone must have cut it before,
while it was still in the boat shed.

371
00:19:44,474 --> 00:19:46,393
But you need a key card to get in.

372
00:19:47,603 --> 00:19:49,646
And we're the only ones
who have key cards.

373
00:19:50,814 --> 00:19:53,192
So that means it was one of us.

374
00:19:58,572 --> 00:20:01,825
All right, who the hell did this?
Show yourself, you traitor.

375
00:20:01,909 --> 00:20:03,493
Busted our asses all season.

376
00:20:03,577 --> 00:20:05,579
-I can't believe one of you did this.
-It wasn't you?

377
00:20:05,662 --> 00:20:07,497
-Why would I do it?
-Why would any of us?

378
00:20:07,581 --> 00:20:10,334
[all arguing]

379
00:20:10,417 --> 00:20:12,878
Everybody calm down. Calm down.

380
00:20:12,961 --> 00:20:14,922
Guys, we can't let this break us apart.

381
00:20:15,005 --> 00:20:17,382
All right? There has to be a team
at the end of this.

382
00:20:17,925 --> 00:20:20,260
Noah and I are gonna figure this out.

383
00:20:20,344 --> 00:20:21,637
-Okay?
-[mysterious music playing]

384
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:23,805
-[Noah] We need to narrow our time frame.
-Mm-hmm.

385
00:20:23,889 --> 00:20:27,643
We were all in the boatshed this morning
between 7:30 and 8:30 a.m.

386
00:20:27,726 --> 00:20:31,730
So the sabotage must have happened
after that. Between 8:30 and 9:30.

387
00:20:31,813 --> 00:20:34,441
Right, so where was everyone this morning?

388
00:20:34,524 --> 00:20:36,985
Uh, I was outside stretching with Noah.

389
00:20:37,069 --> 00:20:39,446
Me and Crabby were taking selfies
in the erg room.

390
00:20:39,529 --> 00:20:42,574
-I was doing my pre-race meditation.
-Why are we checking alibis?

391
00:20:42,658 --> 00:20:45,702
None of us wanted to lose this race.
There's no motive here.

392
00:20:45,786 --> 00:20:48,080
On the surface, dear Crabby.

393
00:20:48,580 --> 00:20:51,833
So we need to look for the motive
underneath the motive.

394
00:20:53,335 --> 00:20:54,461
What the hell does that mean?

395
00:20:55,754 --> 00:20:59,925
It means, Perry,
we all have our pre-race superstitions.

396
00:21:00,008 --> 00:21:03,136
Our "free speed," so to speak.

397
00:21:03,220 --> 00:21:04,346
Crabby eats pasta.

398
00:21:04,429 --> 00:21:06,723
Baloo does karaoke
when he thinks no one's watching.

399
00:21:06,807 --> 00:21:12,729
-I do not.
-Josh chooses the oar with the pink tape.

400
00:21:14,189 --> 00:21:18,068
So the question we should be asking
isn't, "Who would target the team?"

401
00:21:18,568 --> 00:21:20,696
But, "Who would target…

402
00:21:20,779 --> 00:21:21,697
Josh?"

403
00:21:21,780 --> 00:21:23,240
[tense music playing]

404
00:21:33,542 --> 00:21:38,088
So… someone on the team was targeting me.

405
00:21:39,923 --> 00:21:40,924
Why?

406
00:21:41,591 --> 00:21:42,592
Who?

407
00:21:46,305 --> 00:21:47,514
Oh, come on.

408
00:21:48,598 --> 00:21:49,641
It could've been Baloo.

409
00:21:49,725 --> 00:21:52,019
He's pissed at Josh
'cause he dumped his sister.

410
00:21:52,102 --> 00:21:54,938
Yeah. Should've heard him ranting
about Josh and Britney last night.

411
00:21:55,022 --> 00:21:57,107
-Perry.
-Sorry, Baloo.

412
00:22:00,861 --> 00:22:05,198
You broke up with her on her big night.
What is wrong with you, dude?

413
00:22:06,325 --> 00:22:07,951
Okay, look, I may be pissed,

414
00:22:08,035 --> 00:22:10,120
but that doesn't mean I did it.
What about her?

415
00:22:11,371 --> 00:22:12,372
What?

416
00:22:12,456 --> 00:22:14,791
You and Josh have been
at each other's throats

417
00:22:14,875 --> 00:22:15,751
from the beginning.

418
00:22:20,380 --> 00:22:24,593
That's true, yes.
We have a history, and I do hate him.

419
00:22:24,676 --> 00:22:26,261
But guys, I'm your cox.

420
00:22:26,345 --> 00:22:30,098
-I would never do this.
-And then there's Perry's gripe.

421
00:22:31,058 --> 00:22:33,393
-Dude.
-What? What gripe?

422
00:22:34,227 --> 00:22:35,937
I told you that in confidence, Noah.

423
00:22:36,855 --> 00:22:37,773
What?

424
00:22:40,692 --> 00:22:43,862
That is a 10.01 ash blond.

425
00:22:43,945 --> 00:22:49,659
My base is also a 10.01 ash blond.
You stole my hair color, man.

426
00:22:49,743 --> 00:22:51,203
-My mom picked it for me.
-But…

427
00:22:51,286 --> 00:22:53,705
[Perry] It doesn't matter.
I didn't break the oar, I swear.

428
00:22:53,789 --> 00:22:57,042
What about Cam? Wasn't he also pissed
about the whole stroke thing?

429
00:22:57,125 --> 00:23:00,212
Wow. Thanks, man. What about you?
How do we know you don't have a grudge?

430
00:23:00,295 --> 00:23:01,713
You've never given Josh a piggyback.

431
00:23:01,797 --> 00:23:04,716
Well, yeah, not for lack of trying.

432
00:23:05,258 --> 00:23:06,927
Why do you hate piggybacks, man?

433
00:23:07,552 --> 00:23:10,180
I also have a reason to hate Josh.

434
00:23:14,142 --> 00:23:16,144
Okay, I don't.
I just wanted to be included.

435
00:23:16,228 --> 00:23:18,772
Who could hate this jawline?

436
00:23:18,855 --> 00:23:20,774
Yeah, well, apparently everyone.

437
00:23:23,276 --> 00:23:25,278
[Noah] I'm sorry,
but I'm going to state the obvious.

438
00:23:25,362 --> 00:23:27,948
Ryder has been gunning for Josh
all season.

439
00:23:28,031 --> 00:23:30,867
He swung at him at the clambake.
He got booted from stroke.

440
00:23:30,951 --> 00:23:32,702
Their granddad came to watch the race.

441
00:23:32,786 --> 00:23:35,580
-And Ryder wanted to sabotage Josh.
-Screw you, man.

442
00:23:35,664 --> 00:23:38,583
You think I would tank the race
over some petty cousin drama?

443
00:23:38,667 --> 00:23:40,168
[Perry] But it's not petty, is it?

444
00:23:40,252 --> 00:23:43,088
One of you is going to get crowned
the king of Regis Airlines.

445
00:23:43,588 --> 00:23:44,923
How could you stoop so low?

446
00:23:45,006 --> 00:23:47,300
-I didn't do it!
-Let's search his bag!

447
00:23:47,384 --> 00:23:50,011
-What the hell, Quaid?
-[Perry] Is the saw in there, Ryder?

448
00:23:50,095 --> 00:23:54,391
-You have nothing to fear if innocent.
-No, go ahead. Search it. Fine.

449
00:23:58,687 --> 00:23:59,980
It's not in there, Quaid.

450
00:24:00,480 --> 00:24:01,690
Yeah. I know.

451
00:24:03,358 --> 00:24:04,359
See?

452
00:24:04,901 --> 00:24:07,988
And just for the record,
I don't want Josh to lose.

453
00:24:08,655 --> 00:24:09,739
I wanna beat him.

454
00:24:10,532 --> 00:24:13,452
In broad daylight. In front of everybody.

455
00:24:18,165 --> 00:24:19,458
Do you believe him?

456
00:24:22,794 --> 00:24:26,173
[clears throat] Well, one way to find out.

457
00:24:26,256 --> 00:24:28,550
There's a security camera
pointed at the sheds.

458
00:24:28,633 --> 00:24:31,928
The footage is on Coach's laptop.
It'll show us who got in.

459
00:24:33,722 --> 00:24:36,349
One of you. Please, go jailbreak it.

460
00:24:36,433 --> 00:24:37,309
[snaps]

461
00:24:37,809 --> 00:24:40,187
-Great. Perry, go!
-[Perry] Me? Why?

462
00:24:40,270 --> 00:24:41,938
I don't know how to hack a computer.

463
00:24:42,022 --> 00:24:43,440
So youtube it!

464
00:24:43,523 --> 00:24:45,567
-But there's so many ads.
-Dude!

465
00:24:46,318 --> 00:24:49,404
-Okay, fine. I'll go pay for premium.
-[Teagan] Thank you.

466
00:24:49,488 --> 00:24:52,824
And the rest of you, go. Look for the saw.

467
00:24:52,908 --> 00:24:56,119
Noah and I
are going to process the evidence.

468
00:24:56,203 --> 00:24:57,871
Go! Come on.

469
00:25:02,209 --> 00:25:03,210
No.

470
00:25:16,932 --> 00:25:19,976
-What are you doing?
-[Josh] Oh, uh, I'm looking for the saw.

471
00:25:20,060 --> 00:25:23,230
Nothing yet,
but I did find an oyster shucker.

472
00:25:24,356 --> 00:25:27,025
You're not here for the oyster shucker,
are you?

473
00:25:28,610 --> 00:25:31,321
Who do you think we're gonna see
on security camera footage?

474
00:25:33,698 --> 00:25:35,075
[Josh] The whole team?

475
00:25:35,158 --> 00:25:37,327
[Teagan] Come on.
Who do you think did this?

476
00:25:38,370 --> 00:25:39,454
Uh…

477
00:25:41,790 --> 00:25:46,670
I mean, could be Baloo.
He's madder than I thought.

478
00:25:47,963 --> 00:25:49,422
Could be Cam.

479
00:25:49,506 --> 00:25:52,008
Cam? Why?

480
00:25:52,509 --> 00:25:54,678
We kind of got into it this morning.

481
00:25:55,720 --> 00:25:57,097
About what?

482
00:25:58,306 --> 00:25:59,933
His sunglasses were broken.

483
00:26:00,016 --> 00:26:02,185
Said he needed a new pair,
and he flipped out.

484
00:26:02,852 --> 00:26:07,065
He has been on edge lately.
But it couldn't be Cam, could it?

485
00:26:10,527 --> 00:26:11,403
Hm…

486
00:26:12,404 --> 00:26:15,115
I mean, I guess it makes sense.
Yeah, Coach pulled Ryder,

487
00:26:15,198 --> 00:26:17,659
but put you in stroke
when it should have been him. So…

488
00:26:18,368 --> 00:26:19,619
[ominous music playing]

489
00:26:19,703 --> 00:26:25,041
Wait. You think
Cam should be in stroke instead of me?

490
00:26:26,835 --> 00:26:29,629
I didn't mean it like that.

491
00:26:29,713 --> 00:26:32,716
No, it's okay. You can be honest with me.

492
00:26:33,508 --> 00:26:34,551
Josh.

493
00:26:39,264 --> 00:26:41,725
Well, yeah, he-he deserves it.

494
00:26:44,185 --> 00:26:45,186
But how come?

495
00:26:45,270 --> 00:26:46,396
Come on.

496
00:26:48,648 --> 00:26:50,233
Okay, Cam puts the team first.

497
00:26:50,317 --> 00:26:52,402
You know, no ego, no personal agenda.

498
00:26:52,485 --> 00:26:54,487
He really pulls for the boat.

499
00:26:54,571 --> 00:26:56,031
And I don't?

500
00:26:57,657 --> 00:27:00,160
-Well…
-Is that how everyone sees me?

501
00:27:01,536 --> 00:27:02,662
Even you?

502
00:27:04,539 --> 00:27:07,292
I see that you're trying to prove
you're a different Josh.

503
00:27:07,375 --> 00:27:09,419
So you think
I'm good enough to make out with,

504
00:27:09,502 --> 00:27:11,171
but not good enough for stroke?

505
00:27:12,505 --> 00:27:14,299
-I didn't mean that.
-Nah.

506
00:27:15,717 --> 00:27:16,718
I think you did.

507
00:27:26,311 --> 00:27:29,230
[comically intriguing music playing]

508
00:27:32,692 --> 00:27:34,110
[bottles clattering]

509
00:27:34,194 --> 00:27:35,737
Bunch of scofflaws.

510
00:27:35,820 --> 00:27:37,864
[Teagan] Okay, where were we?

511
00:27:37,947 --> 00:27:38,907
[bottles clatter]

512
00:27:38,990 --> 00:27:42,369
-What's that?
-Quaid set up a speakeasy in the erg room.

513
00:27:42,452 --> 00:27:45,038
The guys were out there partying
instead of looking for the saw.

514
00:27:45,121 --> 00:27:46,581
So you confiscated it?

515
00:27:47,248 --> 00:27:49,668
Actually, those are empties.

516
00:27:49,751 --> 00:27:50,919
I'm helping them recycle.

517
00:27:53,213 --> 00:27:54,547
Everyone hates my party.

518
00:27:55,215 --> 00:27:58,885
Noah, come on. Your… Your party's fun.

519
00:27:58,968 --> 00:28:01,888
Yeah, really? So given the choice
between a night at Quaid's bar

520
00:28:01,971 --> 00:28:03,848
or a night at my murder mystery?

521
00:28:05,225 --> 00:28:06,601
I'd do a murder mystery.

522
00:28:07,519 --> 00:28:10,355
-Lies.
-It's… It's cool.

523
00:28:10,438 --> 00:28:13,817
Okay? It's just,
you know, the wrong crowd.

524
00:28:13,900 --> 00:28:16,027
Oh great. So now I can't read the room.

525
00:28:16,111 --> 00:28:20,407
It's not that.
It's just we're not puzzle people.

526
00:28:20,490 --> 00:28:22,450
The only thing we have in common is crew.

527
00:28:23,410 --> 00:28:26,413
If we weren't in a boat together,
we probably wouldn't be friends.

528
00:28:27,580 --> 00:28:29,290
Wow, you suck at pep talks.

529
00:28:29,958 --> 00:28:33,670
Hey, but that's what's cool
about being a part of a team, you know?

530
00:28:33,753 --> 00:28:39,384
You get to be exposed
to everybody's interesting interests.

531
00:28:39,467 --> 00:28:41,094
And, um…

532
00:28:42,303 --> 00:28:47,809
No, Noah, people who wouldn't be
your people become your people.

533
00:28:48,309 --> 00:28:49,853
Just give it time.

534
00:28:51,020 --> 00:28:52,021
Okay.

535
00:28:52,522 --> 00:28:57,861
Besides, you are really fricking good
at this mystery stuff, okay? We need you.

536
00:28:57,944 --> 00:29:01,156
If Perry can't figure out
the security camera footage,

537
00:29:01,239 --> 00:29:03,533
we'll need to figure this out
ourselves, okay?

538
00:29:03,616 --> 00:29:06,035
So… where are we?

539
00:29:06,119 --> 00:29:07,620
[suspenseful music playing]

540
00:29:07,704 --> 00:29:14,461
Okay. Well, Quaid and I
were stretching outside this morning.

541
00:29:14,544 --> 00:29:15,462
Mm-hmm.

542
00:29:15,545 --> 00:29:18,673
Perry and Crabby
were taking selfies in the erg room.

543
00:29:18,757 --> 00:29:20,258
Mm-hmm.

544
00:29:28,057 --> 00:29:29,058
Hold on.

545
00:29:30,185 --> 00:29:31,186
What?

546
00:29:33,646 --> 00:29:37,025
Cam said he was stretching
in the erg room before the race, right?

547
00:29:37,525 --> 00:29:39,569
But this photo was taken in the erg room.

548
00:29:40,069 --> 00:29:41,070
He's not in it.

549
00:29:44,741 --> 00:29:46,659
Cam lied.

550
00:29:52,040 --> 00:29:53,082
Hey.

551
00:29:54,959 --> 00:29:55,960
No sign of the saw.

552
00:29:57,003 --> 00:30:00,340
You know how you said you were
stretching in the erg room earlier?

553
00:30:00,423 --> 00:30:01,633
Yeah.

554
00:30:01,716 --> 00:30:05,512
Perry and Crabcatcher were too,
and, you know, they didn't see you.

555
00:30:05,595 --> 00:30:07,430
Well, I was just in the corner. So.

556
00:30:10,350 --> 00:30:11,684
Which corner?

557
00:30:14,437 --> 00:30:15,522
Wait, you think I did it?

558
00:30:17,273 --> 00:30:19,192
Yeah, I don't… I don't know, Cam.

559
00:30:19,859 --> 00:30:22,821
I mean, you have been
acting different lately.

560
00:30:22,904 --> 00:30:26,491
You walked out at the dance. No one knows
where you were during the sabotage.

561
00:30:26,574 --> 00:30:29,118
-What am I supposed to think?
-That I'm the Cam you know.

562
00:30:29,202 --> 00:30:30,954
The one who'd never sabotage the team.

563
00:30:31,037 --> 00:30:34,249
Yeah, but the Cam I know
wouldn't pick a fight with Josh, either.

564
00:30:36,292 --> 00:30:38,336
How did you know
I got in a fight with Josh?

565
00:30:38,419 --> 00:30:40,213
We were the only people there.

566
00:30:42,507 --> 00:30:43,758
He told me.

567
00:30:44,551 --> 00:30:45,552
Right.

568
00:30:46,344 --> 00:30:48,054
You guys are pretty close now, huh?

569
00:30:48,680 --> 00:30:51,266
-We're not that close.
-Close enough that he's sharing.

570
00:30:51,766 --> 00:30:53,351
You wanna know what I was doing?

571
00:30:54,519 --> 00:30:58,690
I was selling my dad's truck
to one of the Westvale rowers.

572
00:31:00,149 --> 00:31:04,195
-Cam. Why didn't you just tell me that?
-Because it's no one's business.

573
00:31:04,279 --> 00:31:06,155
[melancholy music playing]

574
00:31:06,239 --> 00:31:08,074
You really think I'd do this to him?

575
00:31:09,909 --> 00:31:11,494
Yeah, you don't know me at all.

576
00:31:16,374 --> 00:31:17,333
[Perry] Huddle up.

577
00:31:17,417 --> 00:31:24,173
I'm in. And here we go.

578
00:31:28,136 --> 00:31:29,929
Teagan did her morning checks.

579
00:31:30,013 --> 00:31:32,891
Fast forward.

580
00:31:34,350 --> 00:31:36,644
You didn't mention Josh was there too.

581
00:31:36,728 --> 00:31:38,396
Uh, he was grabbing gear.

582
00:31:38,479 --> 00:31:40,189
I needed tape and wrap.

583
00:31:41,691 --> 00:31:44,736
Teagan's out 20 minutes later. So's Josh.

584
00:31:44,819 --> 00:31:46,821
A long time to be grabbing gear.

585
00:31:48,781 --> 00:31:49,991
My dad called.

586
00:31:52,118 --> 00:31:53,786
{\an8}Then there's a bunch of nothing…

587
00:31:54,913 --> 00:31:58,207
-Well, guess we've seen enough.
-Wait, there's more.

588
00:32:00,126 --> 00:32:01,127
Baloo?

589
00:32:01,628 --> 00:32:03,838
You didn't mention going to the sheds.

590
00:32:07,884 --> 00:32:10,219
{\an8}That's a Westvale duffel bag.

591
00:32:10,303 --> 00:32:12,805
{\an8}Baloo, what are you doing
with a Westvale rower?

592
00:32:12,889 --> 00:32:15,642
And what were you doing with him
in boat storage?

593
00:32:15,725 --> 00:32:17,435
What do you think I was doing?

594
00:32:17,518 --> 00:32:20,355
So Thirst Trap Guy's a Westvale rower.

595
00:32:20,438 --> 00:32:21,981
You're dating the enemy.

596
00:32:22,065 --> 00:32:24,525
[Perry] Hang on. There's more footage.

597
00:32:27,612 --> 00:32:31,157
{\an8}-You left him in there alone?
-[dramatic music playing]

598
00:32:35,536 --> 00:32:36,537
{\an8}[Noah] He has a bag.

599
00:32:36,621 --> 00:32:39,082
{\an8}Could have brought the saw,
cut the oar, and left.

600
00:32:42,669 --> 00:32:44,337
I can't believe he did this.

601
00:32:52,595 --> 00:32:55,765
["From a Different Life, It Seems"
by Alex Banin playing]

602
00:32:57,558 --> 00:32:59,769
I can't believe you used me, Logan.

603
00:33:00,561 --> 00:33:04,816
I thought we had something… real.

604
00:33:06,859 --> 00:33:08,111
I'm an idiot.

605
00:33:10,530 --> 00:33:11,906
Lose my number.

606
00:33:11,990 --> 00:33:17,996
<i>♪ Do you miss when</i>
<i>You would do whatever you would like? ♪</i>

607
00:33:18,079 --> 00:33:20,331
<i>♪ Life is just so different ♪</i>

608
00:33:20,415 --> 00:33:22,417
<i>♪ I don't miss it ♪</i>

609
00:33:23,960 --> 00:33:26,421
<i>♪ But I miss you sometimes ♪</i>

610
00:33:26,504 --> 00:33:28,381
<i>♪ And I never care no more ♪</i>

611
00:33:28,464 --> 00:33:30,466
<i>♪ Just bought a one-way from New York ♪</i>

612
00:33:30,550 --> 00:33:33,136
<i>♪ I'll come back when I can't afford you ♪</i>

613
00:33:33,219 --> 00:33:35,054
<i>♪ Or I'm over it ♪</i>

614
00:33:35,138 --> 00:33:37,140
<i>♪ I never care no more ♪</i>

615
00:33:37,223 --> 00:33:39,225
<i>♪ Bought a one-way from New York ♪</i>

616
00:33:39,308 --> 00:33:42,145
<i>♪ I'll come back when I can't afford you ♪</i>

617
00:33:42,228 --> 00:33:44,230
<i>♪ Or I'm over it ♪</i>

618
00:33:45,064 --> 00:33:50,987
<i>♪ You were setting fires, and I… ♪</i>

619
00:33:53,865 --> 00:33:54,907
Hey.

620
00:33:54,991 --> 00:33:57,493
[all murmuring and comforting]

621
00:34:02,081 --> 00:34:04,792
<i>-♪ Don't do that anymore… ♪</i>
-[phone buzzes]

622
00:34:06,919 --> 00:34:10,298
<i>♪ Don't do that anymore, anymore ♪</i>

623
00:34:10,381 --> 00:34:13,926
<i>-♪ And I never care no more ♪</i>
-[phone vibrating]

624
00:34:14,010 --> 00:34:15,053
I can't.

625
00:34:17,346 --> 00:34:18,431
Come here.

626
00:34:20,600 --> 00:34:21,768
He's blocked.

627
00:34:22,268 --> 00:34:23,352
-Thanks.
-Okay.

628
00:34:25,980 --> 00:34:27,607
I just need a minute.

629
00:34:41,245 --> 00:34:42,497
Hey, man.

630
00:34:43,372 --> 00:34:45,708
The team wanted to send you
emotional support carbs.

631
00:34:47,293 --> 00:34:49,420
Banana chocolate chunk. Your fave.

632
00:34:49,504 --> 00:34:51,089
[Baloo] Leave me alone, Josh.

633
00:34:54,467 --> 00:34:56,511
Hey, look, I know
you don't want to hear from me now,

634
00:34:56,594 --> 00:34:58,262
but I have to tell you something.

635
00:35:00,348 --> 00:35:01,641
I'm sorry.

636
00:35:03,851 --> 00:35:04,977
For what?

637
00:35:11,400 --> 00:35:13,361
Baloo, you've always been
such a good friend to me,

638
00:35:13,444 --> 00:35:15,696
and you don't deserve any of this.

639
00:35:17,365 --> 00:35:18,699
I, uh…

640
00:35:21,035 --> 00:35:22,912
-[Baloo sniffles]
-I…

641
00:35:30,086 --> 00:35:33,297
I can't make any of this better,
and I really wish I could.

642
00:35:33,881 --> 00:35:36,634
[soft music playing]

643
00:35:36,717 --> 00:35:39,428
My sister is my sister,

644
00:35:39,512 --> 00:35:43,808
and I still think you're a piece of shit
for dumping her.

645
00:35:48,729 --> 00:35:50,523
I'm glad we agree on something.

646
00:36:10,751 --> 00:36:13,588
That was crazy. I can't believe
we solved a real-life mystery.

647
00:36:14,088 --> 00:36:15,923
Yeah, I told you it wasn't me.

648
00:36:16,007 --> 00:36:18,718
If it weren't for Teagan and Noah,
you would've kicked me off the team.

649
00:36:18,801 --> 00:36:22,722
That was so intense, man. Also, sorry.

650
00:36:22,805 --> 00:36:24,056
[team apologizing]

651
00:36:24,140 --> 00:36:27,852
Oh… There's news afoot.
Today's rankings just came in.

652
00:36:27,935 --> 00:36:30,605
Lakeview came third,
but Cedarside finished twelfth.

653
00:36:30,688 --> 00:36:31,647
They're out!

654
00:36:31,731 --> 00:36:33,232
We're going to the Haverford Cup.

655
00:36:33,316 --> 00:36:38,404
-Yeah!
-[all cheering]

656
00:36:39,280 --> 00:36:40,865
[Perry] You know what this calls for?

657
00:36:40,948 --> 00:36:42,825
A murder mystery.

658
00:36:43,701 --> 00:36:45,620
Noah, why don't you give us the next clue?

659
00:36:47,538 --> 00:36:48,706
-Seriously?
-[Quaid] Yeah, man.

660
00:36:48,789 --> 00:36:51,167
We can't just leave
a dowager murdered there.

661
00:36:52,585 --> 00:36:56,130
Okay. Um, well, I'll give you a hint.

662
00:36:56,214 --> 00:36:58,841
The oyster shucker
is not the real murder weapon.

663
00:36:58,925 --> 00:37:03,221
And, and… the dowager duchess
isn't actually murdered.

664
00:37:03,304 --> 00:37:04,639
-[Crabcatcher] What?
-[team gasps]

665
00:37:04,722 --> 00:37:06,682
So she… faked her death?

666
00:37:06,766 --> 00:37:08,476
[Cam] She could be
in cahoots with somebody.

667
00:37:08,559 --> 00:37:10,186
[Perry] Cahoots. Good word.

668
00:37:13,397 --> 00:37:14,565
[Teagan] Hm.

669
00:37:16,817 --> 00:37:18,611
I'm guessing you didn't…

670
00:37:18,694 --> 00:37:23,115
You didn't text me so we could pick up on
our make-out session from this morning?

671
00:37:24,158 --> 00:37:25,243
No.

672
00:37:28,579 --> 00:37:30,873
You know, you're right about me.

673
00:37:30,957 --> 00:37:33,876
I, um… I don't do
what's best for the team.

674
00:37:35,670 --> 00:37:38,172
Josh, I didn't mean for it
to come out harsh.

675
00:37:38,256 --> 00:37:39,966
No. It's true though.

676
00:37:40,800 --> 00:37:44,553
I'm selfish, and I hurt people.
Almost everyone had a motive against me.

677
00:37:44,637 --> 00:37:46,722
Yeah, because everybody was in shock.

678
00:37:46,806 --> 00:37:49,183
Okay? They were looking
for someone to blame.

679
00:37:49,267 --> 00:37:50,434
Teagan.

680
00:37:51,644 --> 00:37:53,396
You're not supposed to be with me.

681
00:37:56,148 --> 00:37:58,442
What? Because I said
Cam should be in stroke?

682
00:37:58,526 --> 00:38:01,445
-Because I'm-I'm not a good person.
-Josh.

683
00:38:01,529 --> 00:38:04,115
Look, from the first day we met,
you thought I was an asshole.

684
00:38:04,198 --> 00:38:06,951
-Yeah, but I don't think that anymore.
-Well, I'm not different.

685
00:38:07,034 --> 00:38:09,912
I don't know what you're talking about.
Could you just be honest with me?

686
00:38:09,996 --> 00:38:12,790
-Is that what you want? You want honesty?
-Yeah!

687
00:38:14,875 --> 00:38:17,753
We're both on the rebound,
so let's just cut our losses.

688
00:38:20,673 --> 00:38:22,383
Oh wow.

689
00:38:24,218 --> 00:38:27,430
[somber music playing]

690
00:38:29,056 --> 00:38:31,559
It's good to know how you really feel.

691
00:38:35,146 --> 00:38:36,564
["Passenger" by Sir Chloe playing]

692
00:38:36,647 --> 00:38:41,902
<i>♪ I know I don't remember everything ♪</i>

693
00:38:43,321 --> 00:38:48,576
<i>♪ My passenger, you take away my sleep ♪</i>

694
00:38:50,619 --> 00:38:54,915
<i>♪ I soak my cigarettes in gasoline ♪</i>

695
00:38:57,209 --> 00:39:02,340
<i>♪ I try, there's no relief</i>
<i>There's no relief ♪</i>

696
00:39:04,550 --> 00:39:10,431
<i>♪ Ooh, what do I do? ♪</i>

697
00:39:11,015 --> 00:39:18,022
<i>♪ It happened then</i>
<i>But I still have the wound ♪</i>

698
00:39:18,105 --> 00:39:24,445
<i>♪ Ooh, it's no, no use ♪</i>

699
00:39:24,528 --> 00:39:30,785
<i>♪ My passenger, you ruin my perfume ♪</i>

700
00:39:32,203 --> 00:39:34,789
[Cam] <i>Maybe everything you have,</i>
<i>you don't deserve.</i>

701
00:39:38,417 --> 00:39:42,171
[phone ringing]

702
00:39:42,254 --> 00:39:43,631
Hi, Dr. Monroe.

703
00:39:43,714 --> 00:39:46,342
[Monroe] <i>Josh, your ECG results came back.</i>

704
00:39:46,425 --> 00:39:48,511
<i>Your left ventricle wall has thickened.</i>

705
00:39:49,095 --> 00:39:50,304
What does that mean?

706
00:39:50,388 --> 00:39:54,058
<i>You're going to need surgery.</i>
<i>Until then, no physical activity.</i>

707
00:39:54,141 --> 00:39:56,435
But I have a race today.
My family's watching.

708
00:39:56,519 --> 00:39:59,522
<i>Josh, you are at serious risk</i>
<i>of a heart attack.</i>

709
00:39:59,605 --> 00:40:01,399
<i>Do you understand that?</i>

710
00:40:04,485 --> 00:40:06,445
[rushing sound swells]

711
00:40:06,529 --> 00:40:12,076
<i>♪ Ooh, what do I do? ♪</i>

712
00:40:12,618 --> 00:40:19,500
<i>♪ It happened then</i>
<i>But I still have the wound ♪</i>

713
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:26,173
<i>♪ Ooh, it's no, no use ♪</i>

714
00:40:26,257 --> 00:40:33,222
<i>♪ My passenger, you ruin my perfume ♪</i>

715
00:40:40,271 --> 00:40:42,273
[song ends]

716
00:40:43,691 --> 00:40:45,359
[intriguing music playing]

717
00:41:33,949 --> 00:41:35,951
[music ends]
